1. Problem Statement
Process a 2D matrix of student marks across multiple sequential mid-term examinations, calculate examination averages, identify improvements or performance declines across tests, flag consistently weak subjects (<40 mark average), and classify overall performance trends.

2. Objectives
•	Calculate student-wise and exam-wise average performance.
•	Analyze trajectory (improving, declining, fluctuating).
•	Identify chronically weak subjects requiring remedial attention.

3. Assumptions
•	Assessment marks are stored in chronological order [Exam 1, Exam 2, Exam 3].
•	Consistency is evaluated by comparing consecutive test variations.

4. Algorithm
1. Store marks as nested list: each student row contains list of test scores.
2. For each student, compute mean score across tests.
3. Compare scores: if T3 > T2 > T1 -> 'Improving'; if T3 < T2 < T1 -> 'Declining'; else 'Fluctuating'.
4. Identify tests where average score fell below subject benchmark (40).
5. Generate comprehensive performance summary.
